ve controls including one lymph node obtained from a patient with disease other than breast cancer (LN, lane &#x00023;6) and peripheral blood lymphocytes obtained form healthy volunteers (PBL, lanes &#x00023;7&#x02013;9). Three primary tumours were used as positive controls (TU, lanes &#x00023;10&#x02013;12).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="94-6602992f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Analysis of sentinel lymph nodes for the presence of breast cancer metastases by H&#x00026;E, IHC and RT&#x02013;PCR</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>CK-19</bold></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>NY-BR-1</bold></th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>MGB-2</bold></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>H&#x00026;E</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>IHC</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RT</bold>&#x02013;<bold>PCR</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>SB</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RT</bold>&#x02013;<bold>PCR</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>SB<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>RT</bold>&#x02013;<bold>PCR</bold></th><th align="cent